#!/usr/bin/env xetal
## The landscape: the accounting of the ways to change a layer, each
## figure analytical (it follows from the method's definition, no
## training is run). For two layers, this course's 8 x 8 at rank 4
## and one real layer, 4096 x 4096 at rank 16: for each family whose
## cost is a count, the numbers trained, the numbers held while
## training beyond the weights themselves (the gradient and Adam's two
## averages, where there are any), and the numbers stored afterward
## when the change is kept apart from W. Then the bytes of the layer
## itself at 16 bits and at 4 bits (QLoRA's base), and the adapter's
## share of the full count.

"lo:" u_se< "LoRA"

### Data

## The two layers side by side: d is the width of each (the layer is
## d x d), r the rank an adapter would have on it.
d := 8 4096
r := 4 16
all := d * d
## One row in eight of the layer, the selective case this page takes: an
## eighth of the numbers.
some := f_loor all / 8
## LoRA's count from the library, r (d + d), at each layer.
lora := (4 lo:p_arams 8 8) c_at 16 lo:p_arams 4096 4096

### The numbers trained

## A row per family that has a count, in the order the page lists
## them: full fine-tuning (every number of W); selective fine-tuning
## (here one row in eight); LoRA (A and B); LoRA-FA (B alone); QLoRA
## (LoRA's adapter on a quantized W); DoRA (LoRA's adapter and a
## magnitude per column); VeRA (two vectors, d and r long, on frozen
## shared tables); learning without back-propagation on every weight
## (MeZO); a closed-form rank-one edit (nothing is trained). A column
## per layer.
trained := (9 c_at 2) r_eshape all c_at some c_at lora c_at (r * d) c_at lora c_at (lora + d) c_at (d + r) c_at all c_at 0 0
r_avel trained

### The numbers held while training

## Back-propagation with Adam holds, for every number trained, its
## gradient and two running averages: three more numbers. The
## two-point estimate holds a seed and two losses, no gradient; a
## closed-form edit holds nothing while it trains, since it does not.
held := trained * (3 3 3 3 3 3 3 0 0) '* t_able 1 1
r_avel held

### The numbers stored afterward

## The change kept apart from W: full and selective fine-tuning keep
## the moved numbers; an adapter keeps its tables (LoRA-FA and VeRA
## regrow their frozen ones from a seed); the forward-only method
## moved every weight; a rank-one edit is two vectors, u and v. An
## adapter merged into W is d x d again, the first row.
stored := (9 c_at 2) r_eshape all c_at some c_at lora c_at (r * d) c_at lora c_at (lora + d) c_at (d + r) c_at all c_at 2 * d
r_avel stored

### Bytes and shares

## The layer's own bytes at 16 bits a number and at 4 bits (what
## QLoRA's quantized base takes, before its scales), at each width.
(16 lo:b_ytes all) c_at 4 lo:b_ytes all
## The adapter's share of the full count, LoRA then LoRA-FA.
((f_loat lora) / f_loat all) c_at (f_loat r * d) / f_loat all
